>> how to run one test file and which error format the API uses

=====================================================
Based on the CLAUDE.md documentation in this project:

----------------------
Running one test file:

With vitest, you can run a specific test file by passing the file path:

npm run test:run -- src/routes/orders.test.ts

Or in watch mode:
npm test -- src/routes/orders.test.ts

(Though CLAUDE.md notes: never run npm test in non-interactive contexts — use npm run test:run for CI/verification.)

Error format:

The API uses a standard error shape everywhere:

{
  "error": {
    "code": "string",
    "message": "string",
    "details": "unknown (optional)"
  }
}

Examples from the conventions:
- 400 Validation error: { "error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "..." } }
- 404 Not found: { "error": { "code": "NOT_FOUND", "message": "..." } }
- 500 Unexpected error: generic message only, details logged server-side (never return stack traces)